  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 26 files needed to plan this refactor, ordered by importance:\n\n**spring-kafka (primary implementation, most changes):**\n- `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.java` / `KafkaMessageListenerContainer.java` / `AbstractMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the threading model itself (concurrency, per-partition `KafkaMessageListenerContainer` children, `AsyncTaskExecutor` per child)\n- `ContainerProperties.java`, `MessageListenerContainer.java`, `GenericMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 shared container config/contract\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `AbstractKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `KafkaListenerContainerFactory.java` \u2014 factory wiring that sets `concurrency`\n- `KafkaListenerEndpointRegistry.java`, `KafkaListenerEndpointRegistrar.java` \u2014 lifecycle/registry managing containers as `SmartLifecycle` beans\n- `KafkaListener.java`, `EnableKafka.java`, `KafkaListenerAnnotationBeanPostProcessor.java` \u2014 annotation-driven endpoint creation (concurrency attribute)\n- `ContainerCustomizer.java` \u2014 extension point touched by both spring-kafka and spring-boot\n\n**spring-boot (autoconfiguration/properties consumer):**\n- `KafkaAutoConfiguration.java`, `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration.java` \u2014 wires `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory` as the default bean\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer.java` \u2014 maps `spring.kafka.listener.concurrency` property onto the factory\n- `KafkaProperties.java` \u2014 the `Listener.concurrency` config surface\n\n**spring-framework (core abstractions, upstream dependency):**\n- `AsyncTaskExecutor.java`, `SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor.java`, `TaskExecutor.java` \u2014 the executor abstraction each child container runs on\n- `SmartLifecycle.java`, `Lifecycle.java` \u2014 the phased start/stop contract `MessageListenerContainer` implements\n- `TaskScheduler.java`, `ThreadPoolTaskExecutor.java` \u2014 pooled alternative to the default one-thread-per-consumer executor, relevant to any configurable-concurrency redesign\n\nThis set covers the full chain: framework-level threading/lifecycle primitives \u2192 spring-kafka's container/factory/registry implementation \u2192 spring-boot's property-driven autoconfiguration \u2014 sufficient to derive the dependency graph, ordering constraints, and breaking-change surface (e.g., `KafkaMessageListenerContainer` constructor visibility, `ContainerProperties.listenerTaskExecutor`, and the `KafkaProperties.Listener.concurrency` property contract) needed for `REFACTOR_PLAN.md`.",
